                "evidence": "**Route: Plan.** The argument names it, and the state agrees: no folder under `docs/plans/`, tree clean on `main`, level with `origin/main` at `ee1aea7`.\n\n**Size: Bounded, provisional until research.** One subsystem (the task record and its three thin readers), one PR. Budgets: at most 5 questions total, 1 explorer, `product.md` two pages and `implementation.md` three, tech lead plus at most one seat, 5 to 7 turns to Ready. Two harness notes: the profile's Judge reads `Model: none`, so I judge every gate myself, and the question tool is unavailable, so questions come as written blocks.\n\n**Probe: absent.** `git grep -il -E 'due|deadline|dueDate|due_date' origin/main -- src public migrations scripts tests docs` returned nothing, and `origin/main` is the only remote branch. Closest existing feature is **task priority**: a field at `src/tasks.js:4,6`, backfilled by `migrations/002-add-priority.js:2`, rendered by `src/format.js:13`, filtered at `src/tasks.js:13-14`. That is the template a due date should follow.\n\n**The ask, restated.** A task gains a due date, the page at `GET /` shows it, and `src/cli.js` sets it. Ledger: `docs/plans/task-due-date/decisions.md`, with your three statements locked as D1 to D3 and the repo-answerable frame items (appetite, personas, constraints, stakeholder) recorded as D4 to D7 rather than asked.\n\n**Q1. Does \"every task\" mean the due date is required, or a field every task has that may be empty?**\n\n- **(a) Optional.** Absent means no due date. Buys: no migration, `cli.js add <title>` and `POST /tasks` keep working unchanged, no invented dates. Costs: the page and the CLI each need an \"no due date\" state, and \"every task has a due date\" holds for the field, not the value.\n- **(b) Required with a default,** say seven days out. Buys: one populated state to render everywhere. Costs: a backfill migration over existing tasks, and every task Mara adds carries a deadline she did not pick.\n- **(c) Required, no default.** `add` and `POST /tasks` fail without a date. Buys: no guessed dates. Costs: breaks the existing contract, which Priya's cron job calls with `{title}` only.\n\n**Recommended: (a).** It is the only option that neither breaks `POST /tasks` at `src/server.js:31` nor writes a date nobody chose; priority needed `migrations/002` only because priority is required, and this field does not have to be. This reads your \"every task\" as every task *can* carry one.\n\nReply \"ok\" for (a), or name the letter.\n\nPrinciples applied: 1 (the repo answered appetite, personas, constraints, and the stakeholder, so four frame questions were recorded instead of asked), 2 (one question, with a default), 3 (required-versus-optional is scope, so it is yours), 5 (option (a) adds no migration and no dependency)."
